      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0201",
      "sequence": 213,
      "meaning": "Once Kauśalyā bathed and adorned the child and laid him in his cradle. She bathed for worship, honored the family deity, offered food, and went to the kitchen; returning, she saw her son eating the offering. Frightened, she hurried to the child and found him still asleep, then returned and again saw him eating. Her heart trembled at seeing two children and she wondered whether her mind was confused. Rāma smiled gently at his distressed mother and showed her his wondrous, indivisible form, with millions of universes present in every pore.",
