    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0202",
      "sequence": 214,
      "meaning": "Within Rāma’s cosmic form Kauśalyā saw countless suns, moons, Śivas and Brahmās; many mountains, rivers, oceans, earths and forests; time, action, qualities, knowledge, nature, and things no one had ever heard of. She saw mighty māyā standing terrified with joined hands, the beings whom māyā makes dance, and devotion that frees them. Thrilled and speechless, she closed her eyes and bowed at his feet. The foe of Khara became an infant again. Unable to praise him and awed that she had regarded the world’s father as her son, she listened as Hari reassured her and told her to disclose this nowhere. Joining her hands repeatedly, Kauśalyā begged that his māyā never envelop her again.",
