    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0203",
      "sequence": 215,
      "meaning": "Hari performed many kinds of childhood play and gave his servants immense delight. After some time all four brothers grew and brought happiness to the household. The guru performed their tonsure, and the Brahmins received abundant gifts. The four tender boys roamed about in endlessly charming play: the one beyond mind, action and speech moved through Daśaratha’s courtyard. When the king called him to eat, he would not leave the other children; when Kauśalyā went to fetch him, the Lord toddled away, and the mother stubbornly ran after the one whose limit scripture and Śiva cannot find. He came in covered with dust and Daśaratha laughingly seated him on his lap. At meals the restless child watched for a chance, ran off laughing, his face smeared with curds and rice.",
