    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0204",
      "sequence": 216,
      "meaning": "The children’s innocent, lovely deeds are sung by Sarasvatī, Śeṣa, Śiva and the Vedas; those whose minds do not delight in them have been deprived by fate. When the brothers became boys, guru, father and mother invested them with the sacred thread. Rāma went to the teacher’s home to study and mastered every discipline in little time. Hari, whose natural breath is the four Vedas, studying is a great wonder. Expert in learning and humility and rich in virtue and conduct, the brothers played all the games of princes. Bow and arrow shone beautifully in their hands, and their appearance enchanted all creation. Wherever they walked, men and women stopped in wonder. To every man, woman, elder and child in Ayodhyā, compassionate Rāma was dearer than life.",
