    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0205",
      "sequence": 217,
      "meaning": "The brothers called their companions and regularly went to the forest to play at hunting. Rāma struck game whom he inwardly knew would be sanctified and brought them daily to show the king; animals killed by his arrows left their bodies and reached heaven. The brothers ate with younger brothers and friends and followed their parents’ commands. The treasury of compassion arranged whatever would make the townspeople happy. They listened attentively to Veda and Purāṇa and themselves explained them to their younger brothers. Rising at dawn, Raghunātha bowed his head to mother, father and teacher, then asked leave and carried out the city’s affairs, delighting the king. All-pervading, indivisible, desireless, unborn, attributeless, without name or form, he performed incomparable deeds of many kinds for his devotees.",
